---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Fetch a plugin from a workspace path or an https URL, print its manifest, pin its sha256 and declare it with no grants

Usage: rustman plugin add [OPTIONS] <SOURCE>

Arguments:
  <SOURCE>
          A plugin folder or .wasm file inside the workspace, or an https URL

Options:
      --name <NAME>
          The workspace's name for the plugin (default: the manifest's name)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
